Database Backup Automation
Example: MySQL Production Backup Script
#!/bin/bash

DATE=$(date +%F-%H-%M)

BACKUP_DIR=/backup/mysql

MYSQL_USER=admin
MYSQL_PASSWORD=Admin@123

mkdir -p $BACKUP_DIR

mysqldump -u$MYSQL_USER -p$MYSQL_PASSWORD \
--single-transaction \
--routines \
--triggers \
production_db > $BACKUP_DIR/prod-$DATE.sql

gzip $BACKUP_DIR/prod-$DATE.sql

find $BACKUP_DIR -type f -mtime +7 -delete
6. Explanation of Production-Level Commands
Command	Purpose
mysqldump	Export database
--single-transaction	Avoid DB locking
gzip	Compress backup
find -mtime	Delete old backups
mkdir -p	Create directory safely

